# Helm installation

1. Download and modify the default configuration file [values.yaml](https://github.com/newrelic/helm-charts/blob/master/charts/nr-ebpf-agent/values.yaml#L1-L4). At minimum, you will need populate the `licenseKey` field with a valid New Relic Ingest key and the `cluster` field with the name of the cluster to monitor.

Example:
```
licenseKey: "EXAMPLEINGESTLICENSEKEY345878592NRALL"
cluster: "name-of-cluster-to-monitor"
```

2. Install the helm chart, passing the configuration file created above.
```sh
helm repo add newrelic https://helm-charts.newrelic.com
helm upgrade nr-ebpf-agent newrelic/nr-ebpf-agent -f your-custom-values.yaml -n newrelic --create-namespace --install
```

{{ template "chart.sourcesSection" . }}

## Component configuration

The chart deploys several components with a single install. Each component keeps its default configuration in its own file under [`components/`](https://github.com/newrelic/helm-charts/tree/master/charts/nr-ebpf-agent/components):

| Component | Defaults file | Top-level keys |
|-----------|---------------|----------------|
| eBPF agent DaemonSet | [`components/ebpf-agent.yaml`](https://github.com/newrelic/helm-charts/blob/master/charts/nr-ebpf-agent/components/ebpf-agent.yaml) | `ebpfAgent`, `protocols`, `allDataFilters`, `apmDataFilters`, `networkMetricsDataFilter`, `logDataFilters`, `processStats`, `entityLabels`, `report*`, `logLevel`, `logFilePath`, `genAICaptureMessageContent`, `customOtlpEndpoint*`, `metadataEndpoint`, `metadataTlsCertPath`, `otlpProxy`, `metadataProxy` |
| nrdot collectors + kube-state-metrics | [`components/nrdot.yaml`](https://github.com/newrelic/helm-charts/blob/master/charts/nr-ebpf-agent/components/nrdot.yaml) | `infra`, `nrdotCollector` |
| OpenTelemetry eBPF Instrumentation (OBI) | [`components/obi.yaml`](https://github.com/newrelic/helm-charts/blob/master/charts/nr-ebpf-agent/components/obi.yaml) | `obi` |
| OpenTelemetry eBPF profiler | [`components/profiler.yaml`](https://github.com/newrelic/helm-charts/blob/master/charts/nr-ebpf-agent/components/profiler.yaml) | `profiler` |

`values.yaml` holds only the settings shared by all components (cluster, license key, scheduling, labels, multi-account routing). The values table below lists every option with its default; each component file holds the defaults for its own keys.

The chart merges the component defaults under your values at render time, so you override component keys as usual: in your values file, with `--set`, or under `nr-ebpf-agent:` in a parent chart. Your values always take precedence. To keep your own configuration split by component, pass one file per component in a single command:

```sh
helm upgrade nr-ebpf-agent newrelic/nr-ebpf-agent -n newrelic --create-namespace --install \
  -f common.yaml -f ebpf-agent.yaml -f nrdot.yaml -f obi.yaml -f profiler.yaml
```

## Confirm installation
### Watch pods spin up:

```
kubectl get pods -n newrelic --watch
```

### Check the logs of the eBPF agent pod:
```

# The agent container logs detail probe attachment and data collection.
kubectl logs <ebpf-pod-name> -c nr-ebpf-agent -n newrelic
```

### Confirm data ingest to New Relic
You should see data reporting into New Relic within a couple of seconds to the `Metric` and `Span` tables.
```
FROM Metric SELECT * WHERE k8s.cluster.name='<CLUSTER_NAME>'

FROM Span SELECT * WHERE k8s.cluster.name='<CLUSTER_NAME>'
```
The entities view should show OTel services and an "APM-lite" rendition of the data for each entity when clicked on.

## Uninstall

Run the following command.

```
helm uninstall ebpf-agent -n newrelic
```

## Values managed globally

This chart implements the [New Relic's common Helm library](https://github.com/newrelic/helm-charts/tree/master/library/common-library) which
means that it honors a wide range of defaults and globals common to most New Relic Helm charts.

Options that can be defined globally include `affinity`, `nodeSelector`, `tolerations` and others. The full list can be found at
[user's guide of the common library](https://github.com/newrelic/helm-charts/blob/master/library/common-library/README.md).

